<span class="ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited">Cited by: <a href="#S1.p1.1" title="1. Introduction ‣ Task-Aware Delegation Cues for LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§1</span></a>.
</span></li>
<li id="bib.bib5" class="ltx_bibitem ltx_bib_article"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_bib_author-year ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhang <span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_etal">et al.</span> (2021)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_author">R. Zhang, N. J. McNeese, G. Freeman, and G. Musick</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_title">" An ideal human" expectations of ai teammates in human-ai teaming</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_journal">Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_volume">4</span> (<span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_number">CSCW3</span>), <span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_pages">pp. 1–25</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited">Cited by: <a href="#S1.p1.1" title="1. Introduction ‣ Task-Aware Delegation Cues for LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§1</span></a>.
</span></li>
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Implementation Details: Task Typing and Preference Modeling</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix details the end-to-end implementation of task typing (semantic clustering),
preference alignment, and the two predictive probes (Task A/B) used in Sec. <a href="#S4" title="4. Experiments: Validating Task-Conditioned Collaboration Signals ‣ Task-Aware Delegation Cues for LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
Our goal is reproducibility: we specify inputs, preprocessing, hyperparameters, and evaluation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1. </span>Inputs and data representation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume a dataset of prompts and pairwise preference comparisons:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\{p_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N},\qquad\mathcal{D}=\{(p_{i},m_{A},m_{B},y_{i})\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\{p_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N},\qquad\mathcal{D}=\{(p_{i},m_{A},m_{B},y_{i})\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in\{m_{A},m_{B},\mathrm{tie},\mathrm{invalid}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>tie</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>invalid</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in\{m_{A},m_{B},\mathrm{tie},\mathrm{invalid}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each prompt is assigned a task type <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> via semantic clustering (Sec. <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2. Semantic embedding and task clustering ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details: Task Typing and Preference Modeling ‣ Task-Aware Delegation Cues for LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>),
and comparisons are aligned to clusters for computing task-conditioned statistics (Sec. <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3. Preference alignment and signal computation ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details: Task Typing and Preference Modeling ‣ Task-Aware Delegation Cues for LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2. </span>Semantic embedding and task clustering</h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt embeddings.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We embed each prompt using a pretrained sentence encoder <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathrm{enc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>enc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathrm{enc}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Sentence-BERT):</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}=f_{\mathrm{enc}}(p_{i})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>enc</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}=f_{\mathrm{enc}}(p_{i})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dimensionality reduction.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To improve clusterability and reduce noise, we apply a standard manifold learning operator <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>
(e.g., UMAP) to obtain <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=g(e_{i})\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=g(e_{i})\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}\ll d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≪</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}\ll d</annotation></semantics></math>.
For completeness, UMAP optimizes a cross-entropy objective that preserves neighborhood structure; we
refer to the UMAP paper for the full derivation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Clustering.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We run <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-means on <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=30</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain clusters <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\min_{\{C_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}}\ \sum_{j=1}^{K}\sum_{x_{i}\in C_{j}}\|x_{i}-\mu_{j}\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\min_{\{C_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}}\ \sum_{j=1}^{K}\sum_{x_{i}\in C_{j}}\|x_{i}-\mu_{j}\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the centroid of cluster <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To reduce fragmentation, clusters with size below a threshold <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> are reassigned to the nearest
large cluster by centroid distance:</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{target}}=\arg\min_{j\in\mathcal{L}}\|\mu_{\mathrm{small}}-\mu_{j}\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>target</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>small</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{target}}=\arg\min_{j\in\mathcal{L}}\|\mu_{\mathrm{small}}-\mu_{j}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> indexes clusters with size <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Cluster presentation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For interpretability in the UI/protocol layer, we optionally attach a short label to each cluster
via representative keywords (e.g., top-frequency tokens after standard text preprocessing).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3. </span>Preference alignment and signal computation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each comparison <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{i},m_{A},m_{B},y_{i})\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{i},m_{A},m_{B},y_{i})\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is aligned to the cluster of its prompt <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We compute two task-conditioned signals used in Sec. <a href="#S3" title="3. Preference-Derived Collaboration Signals ‣ Task-Aware Delegation Cues for LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Capability profile (win-rate).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each model <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and cluster <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{m,c}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{m,c}|}\sum_{(i,y_{i})\in\mathcal{D}_{m,c}}\mathbb{I}[y_{i}=m]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m,c}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{m,c}|}\sum_{(i,y_{i})\in\mathcal{D}_{m,c}}\mathbb{I}[y_{i}=m],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{m,c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{m,c}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes comparisons involving <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> whose prompt has <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=c</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Coordination-risk cue (tie-rate).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We quantify task-conditioned uncertainty/disagreement via the cluster tie-rate:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{c}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{c}|}\sum_{(i,y_{i})\in\mathcal{D}_{c}}\mathbb{I}[y_{i}=\mathrm{tie}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>tie</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{c}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}_{c}|}\sum_{(i,y_{i})\in\mathcal{D}_{c}}\mathbb{I}[y_{i}=\mathrm{tie}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> contains all comparisons with <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=c</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the main paper, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is treated as a coordination-risk proxy rather than a ground-truth hardness label.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4. </span>Pipeline pseudocode</h3>

<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> End-to-end Pipeline: Task Typing <math id="alg2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Preference Signals <math id="alg2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Validation Probes</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Prompts </span><math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\{p_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒫</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\{p_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; pairwise comparisons </span><math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}=\{(p_{i},m_{A},m_{B},y_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℛ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}=\{(p_{i},m_{A},m_{B},y_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> with </span><math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in\{m_{A},m_{B},\mathrm{tie},\mathrm{invalid}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">tie</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">invalid</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in\{m_{A},m_{B},\mathrm{tie},\mathrm{invalid}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; encoder </span><math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathrm{enc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">enc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathrm{enc}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; reducer </span><math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (e.g., UMAP); </span><math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> clusters; CV folds </span><math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Task labels </span><math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; capability profiles </span><math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{m,c}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{m,c}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; coordination-risk cues </span><math id="alg2.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{d_{c}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{d_{c}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; CV metrics for Task A/B
</span>
</div>
